WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.860
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:12.990
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.250
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.790
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.300
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:34.140
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.310
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.150
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:45.070
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:52.530
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.540
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.960
Won't go away

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.790
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.930
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.520
Malay Railway

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:09.440
The Malays, Javanese, Indians, and Chinese.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.440
The Red Sun soars high above the numerous ethnic groups here.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.110
While most of the natives act as if they don't see the Japanese,

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:18.240
others show deep respect for them.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.620
This is... a colonized land.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:49.270
Singa... No, Shonan-To is another 6 hours from here.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.560
I'm so used to air-conditioning, this heat is getting to me.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.770
A second-class carriage should still be tolerable.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.610
Or would you prefer the sardine packed style of a third class one?

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:02.410
You managed to get me a hat, shoes and a decent suit.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:03.950
I'm surprised.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.410
Under Martial Law, providing for the ruling authority...

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.580
...brings one many privileges.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.670
No way! No way!

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:13.210
Those without a permit pass are not allowed to take the train!

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.920
All suspicious fellas will be taken to the Military Police, you hear?!

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:22.760
The forceful assertion of authority will not win the people over.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:25.300
That was proven in the post war history.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.640
I'm sure you've learnt that, too.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.980
Can I sit here?

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.560
Excuse me.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.860
It's so hot here... I'm melting.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.950
The Japanese Army is so formidable.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.950
Even "Fortress Singapore" was taken in a flash.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:04.090
I have some business dealings with the army myself.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.260
Recently, I did hear of a little rumor, though.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.970
That during the recent Midway incident,

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.100
quite a number of our planes have been taken down...

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.600
Is the Navy side still okay?

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.190
We're alright.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.520
Japan will definitely win this war.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:23.610
T-That's good. Straight from a Navy Commander himself!

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.680
Should you be sleeping?

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.720
You were sent here to keep an eye on me, right?

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.600
As long as you don't try to jump off from a moving train,

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.900
I'll have plenty more chances when we reach Shonan-To, right?

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.440
What's more, the enemy is everywhere.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.870
What, what's this? It's not even the station yet?!

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.670
A breakdown?

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:21.170
No... Military Police! It's an inspection!

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.630
For anti-Japanese guerillas?

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.930
Or maybe the Chinese rebels.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:32.430
I heard that Military inspections are very strict.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:35.810
Those who're captured seldom come back in one piece.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:37.730
Kusa...

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:42.440
Hey, where's the officer sitting here?

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.820
He went somewhere just a while ago.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.490
He went off? When was that?!

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.780
2-3 minutes ago, I think.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.410
Kusaka!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.830
Everyone! Show your permit pass!

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.920
And your ID too!

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:08.260
This is bad. The permit pass and identification's all with Kusaka.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.890
Let me see it.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.180
Alright.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.100
Okay. Next!

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.150
Alright!

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.900
Let me see it.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.070
Hurry up with it!

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.570
Thanks for your hard work.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.710
What about you?

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:40.630
What's the matter? You don't have them?!

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.250
I'm sorry, but I don't have them.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:44.340
What?

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.460
I'm with the military.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.300
I'm on a classified Intelligence mission...

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.220
...along with a Navy Lieutenant Commander.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.010
The Lieutenant will be able to prove my identity.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.350
The details are... classified.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:59.270
Why you! What are you playing at?!

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:03.770
And? Where's this lieutenant you're on the mission with?

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.940
Well, I have no idea.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.780
He went off somewhere while I was sleeping.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:11.320
I tried looking for him, but...

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.320
Hey!

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.330
Is this man here telling us the truth?

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.790
Huh?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.790
I don't know of any Navy officers on board.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.290
H-Hey!

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:28.920
I thought this man was pretty suspicious myself.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.510
I want you to hand that thing around your waist to me!

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.310
Hand it over now!

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.400
Yamahana Hideo, alias, Yoh Bun Gen!

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.940
You're under arrest as an anti-Japanese spy!

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:46.730
I don't understand?!

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:51.780
Hold it right there!

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.910
Give chase! Get him!

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.030
Yes!

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.750
You're coming back with us to the headquarters.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:04.750
You're gonna tell me all about that man, Yoh!

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.500
I am Japanese!

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.130
I only happened to share a seat with that man!

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:12.430
Being with a Lieutenant Commander for a classified mission...

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:14.640
Do you think you can get away with that ridiculous lie?!

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.260
Stand up!

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:27.940
Is there something you want to ask me?

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.440
Oh... no!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.150
So everything's fine then?

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.950
Yes! Sorry to disturb you!

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:36.410
Keep it up.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.960
And where have you been?!

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.880
I went to look for the banana peddler in the third class carriage.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:53.380
I didn't expect...

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:57.180
...to run into an inspection on this train.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:58.930
What you did will draw unnecessary attention...

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.930
...for a Lieutenant Commander!

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.850
Why didn't you tell me instead?

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:07.310
Because you looked so exhausted from the heat and the tension.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.360
I think you should eat something. This Malayan produce is good.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.500
That wasn't fired from a military rifle.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.710
Yes.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:31.300
To retrieve information, it's a golden rule to capture spies alive.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.050
And knowing how harsh the interrogation of the military is,

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:37.640
suicide is actually a wiser option.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:50.980
A cruiser that reaches 30 knots in speed in just 5 minutes?

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:56.070
And an autogyro that surpasses our military fighter plane?

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:59.030
It sounds too much like a dream.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.700
And you say it bore the rising sun of Japan?

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.700
Who was the one who saw it?

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:06.870
The Ogasawara deployment, Type 2 Fighter Seaplane Pilots.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.080
Not forgetting,

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.290
Commander-in-Chief, Isoroku Yamamoto.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:15.510
It appeared in Ogasawara, and was reported to have gone south.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:18.510
It's most likely in the waters of Singapore right now.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:22.180
Also, it's a personal concern of mine,

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.890
but there's a certain officer whose death isn't confirmed.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:34.440
Shipping and Freight Association.
Shonan City Branch

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:37.400
A 10,000 ton tanker, you say?

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.410
As the Navy's vessels are all involved in other operations,

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:43.700
we'd like to make use of a civilian vessel instead.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:46.700
This is the permit document issued by the local headquarters,

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:49.290
and the official order from the Imperial Navy.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:51.290
Thank you very much.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.600
It's not a problem.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:06.470
Right now, the only vessel that meets the requirements stated,

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:09.480
is the <i>Toshin Maru</i> from "Toyo Steamships",

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:13.690
However, the <i>Toshin Maru</i> just came back from Penang yesterday.

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:17.480
It still requires cleaning, and the crew needs to rest.

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.280
Complete preparations for the ship's departure...

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:21.860
...should take up to about 10 days.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:23.990
I'd like to set out in 5 days.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:29.370
Just my opinion, but 10 days is the least it should take.

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:33.500
This operation involves the lives of many Japanese people.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.790
B-But...

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:36.380
I guess you didn't hear me?

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.420
In 5 days time.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.880
We will do our very best.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.550
A word of advice.

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:47.970
Don't breathe a word about this operation to anyone else.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.230
There's a possibility that our conversations are being tapped,

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:53.020
so phone calls are banned.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:54.650
Is that okay?

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.020
Yes!

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:01.820
So 5 days later, we'll be waiting for you at the Shonan City 3rd Harbor.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:04.700
Yes! T-Thank you for your efforts!

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.910
What's left now is the ship's fuel and food supplies.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:15.540
Following that, the workers to help load the ship.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:18.050
Next, is the Nippon Port Association.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:24.260
This is what they call Martial Law...

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.930
The authority of the Military is invincible.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:44.280
The man named Kusaka... From what I see,

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:48.410
he's a gentlemen, without any arrogance of a military personnel.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:52.540
However, he must be hiding something deep within his heart.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.830
Ever since he read about Japan's future in Mirai's library,

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:59.130
something about him changed.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.630
Kusaka's real intentions...

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:05.090
how should I approach this important issue?

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:08.930
Mr. Kadomatsu, are you ready to go?

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:11.560
Yes, I am.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:15.980
However, isn't it dangerous to be roaming the streets?

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.940
Navy personnel are all over the place...

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.990
It'll be fine.

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:25.780
Right now, no one from the local headquarters...

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.780
or the vessels stationed here has ever seen my face.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:32.370
I double checked that from the war records of your ship's library.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.120
Come, let's go.

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.960
There's a Japan you don't know of out there.

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:03.190
This reminds me of the time I was attached to the British Embassy.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:07.070
It's dazzling. On an island country as small as this,

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:09.780
the Japanese Occupation extends this deep.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:11.950
The liberation of Asia,

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.160
"A New Order in the Far East!"

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:15.620
It sounds good in words,

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:19.080
but what Japan had wanted wasn't the respect of the Asians,

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.750
but the immense natural resources it held.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:26.130
Japan merely replaced the Western powers in exploitation.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.380
After taking North Korea and Taiwan,

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:32.510
Japan invaded into China with liberation as the excuse.

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:36.310
The gap in their actions and words didn't manage to fool the Asians.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:39.770
When did they start to lose their own values,

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:41.360
the Japanese people?

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:51.530
Would you like to see the 21st Century?

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.540
If I had died upon that ocean,

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:07.130
I would never have had the chance to see the 21st Century.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:10.300
If I'm lucky, it'll be another 68 years.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.800
If I live to be a hundred, I'll be able to see it.

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:15.760
I'd like to see it.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:17.770
However,

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:21.810
I have no interest in the 21st Century that you came from.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.360
It's out at last.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:36.080
You want to make a different 21st Century with your own hands?

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.870
I don't think I can accomplish that alone.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:44.130
But, if all outcomes have a reason,

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:47.380
and everything that happens has a meaning to it...

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:51.470
Then why have I survived, Mr. Kadomatsu?

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:54.890
What did you come here to do?

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:59.680
Look, we have an invitation.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:02.440
Would you be my escort for the evening?

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:07.940
You mean... me?

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.620
If it's the tango, I practiced a little some time ago.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.990
Oh my, I love the tango too!

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:23.000
I'm Teruko from the Shonan House. Pleased to meet you.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:31.630
Unrefined, but nonetheless a kind man.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.220
Tsuda?!

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:45.480
According to the records on Mirai,

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:48.110
he should not be in Singapore right now!

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:51.570
Excuse me.

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:58.120
With the appearance of that ship,

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:00.740
history has already begun to change?!

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:16.590
I'm so glad, you're still alive!

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.800
Lieutenant Takumi Kusaka!

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:23.060
I never imagined seeing you again in a place like this!

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:27.690
It's been a month since you left <i>Kirishima</i> in a seaplane.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:29.360
Just where have you been all this time?

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:33.240
I'm sorry... But do I know you?

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:37.030
You seem to have mistaken me for someone else.

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.820
Have you forgotten who I am?

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.330
I'm Kazuma Tsuda, Lieutenant Kusaka!

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:45.910
I'm very sorry, but...

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:49.790
I'm not the Navy Officer that you're looking for.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.300
Excuse me.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:55.840
I'm sorry about that!

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.640
I thought you said you didn't know anyone in Singapore?

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.980
It should have been so.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.030
Should I bring him back?

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:21.120
No. I want you to follow them.

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:23.370
- Keep an eye on them.
- Yes, sir!

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.370
Former subordinate?

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:31.920
Navy Officer, 58th class.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:34.130
He's three classes below me.

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:37.380
Kazuma Tsuda. A superb communications officer.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.720
Why is that man in a place like this?

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:43.680
According to Mirai's records, after Tsuda returned from Midway,

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:46.350
he worked for the Military Command in the local HQ.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.230
What could have happened?

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.560
From what I see, the most likely explanation,

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:54.150
is that he's sent here on special orders.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.610
- Special orders?
- I'm afraid,

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.450
he might be searching for Mirai.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:01.950
We can assume that the upper authorities who spotted Mirai...

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.950
...during Midway have formed a special investigation unit.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:11.330
So we're officially being pursued, I guess.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:13.250
It's not just that.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:18.010
The key personnel and war strategies have greatly changed.

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:21.470
Yet the conditions and crew on Mirai hasn't changed one bit.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:23.470
What're you saying?

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:27.470
The current flow of time and history...

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:30.100
doesn't lead back to you people.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:34.310
No way?!

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:37.480
What about the 21st Century that we came from?!

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:41.490
This place is different from the world you're familiar with.

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:44.160
And a different history will be unfolding.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.210
Stop the carriage.

00:19:56.510 --> 00:20:00.260
High Grade Japanese Sweets Store

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.800
Let's take a walk. It'll help you calm down.

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:14.280
Taki Western Clothing Shop

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:13.980
It's just like a street in Japan.

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:16.270
With the Bakufu's opening of the country,

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:18.980
many people ventured out of Japan to do business.

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:25.070
If we lose our connections with the world we came from,

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.950
will we become grass without roots?!

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:28.910
Or will we become ghosts?!

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:32.790
You're not the only one.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.710
First, I go missing.

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:38.800
And now, I can't even tell my name to a former subordinate of mine.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:51.520
How can...

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:53.600
...that be...

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:56.230
How is that possible?!

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:10.990
I see that you're bleeding, and my fist is still hurting.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.500
We aren't just ghosts!

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.500
I see.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:20.670
Wha... What?!

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:27.180
Hey! What do you think you're doing in front of my shop?!

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:31.310
You filthy drunkards! I'm gonna get the Military Police!

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:33.600
Sorry, sorry.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.560
It's okay.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:39.060
We're definitely not ghosts.

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:41.150
People can still see us.

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:49.120
It's two more days to departure on the <i>Toshin Maru</i>.

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:51.490
Mirai is waiting for us.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:17.240
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:22.480
Just peacefully

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:34.250
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.420 --> 00:22:47.170
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.670 --> 00:22:53.770
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.340 --> 00:22:59.850
I kept on praying

00:23:01.250 --> 00:23:11.690
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:27.370
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.050 --> 00:23:42.050
Supplies aside, if we keep this up...

00:23:42.050 --> 00:23:44.890
it'll evolve into the worst battle between the Japanese.

00:23:44.890 --> 00:23:47.060
Your skills have improved, Tsuda.

00:23:47.060 --> 00:23:49.690
At present, we are the ones who hold the authority.

00:23:49.690 --> 00:23:52.940
It is possible for me to issue an order to seize your ship.

00:23:52.940 --> 00:23:56.530
Why you! Which world are you living in right now?!

00:23:56.530 --> 00:23:59.110
Lieutenant Kusaka, please let me see it.

00:23:59.110 --> 00:24:00.610
I want to see you in action.

00:23:59.990 --> 00:24:04.960
Next Episode: The Pursuer

00:24:00.610 --> 00:24:03.990
The one who creates history is not God. It's mankind.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:09.960
This story is purely fiction. The names of the
characters and organizations that appear have no
connections with actual people and organizations.
